<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-F005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-F005" ;
  triage:title "The variant seam cannot deliver the claim 'a future local model adds a variant, a module a" ;
  triage:description "The variant seam cannot deliver the claim 'a future local model adds a variant, a module and one schema_for arm; no caller signature changes'. schema_for(ModelFamily) returns only a DecisionSchemaId. DecisionSchema has an associated const and associated types and no receiver, so it is not object-safe and has no runtime lookup from DecisionSchemaId or ModelFamily to an implementation. Backends choose at runtime by the model's family. Each new family therefore needs a hand-written match in every consumer (llm::v1::parse_output hard-wires Canonical). The static-vs-dynamic dispatch intent is not stated. Recommendation: State that dispatch is static and keyed by SchemaFamily. Add one object-safe dispatch function in sc-decision-schema, e.g. llm::parse_output(id: DecisionSchemaId, text, payload), that is the only match on SchemaFamily. New families then edit that crate only. Alternatively drop the trait until a second variant exists and keep Canonical as plain functions." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBP" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
